---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="AI & Data Engineering Consultant who loves deep hands-on coding with Python and ML"
	pubDate={new Date('2024-01-01')}
>
	<h2>Hey, I'm Pascal</h2>

	<p>
		I'm an AI & Data Engineering Consultant at Deloitte Consulting in Germany, based around Frankfurt.
		But if I'm being honest, what I really am is someone who loves deep hands-on coding with Python and AI.
		The consulting title is nice, but I'm happiest when I'm actually building things.
	</p>

	<h3>Background</h3>

	<p>
		I studied Computer Science at TU Darmstadt for both my bachelor's and master's. My bachelor's thesis
		looked at explainability in sentence transformers (basically trying to understand what these models
		are actually learning). For my master's, I worked on AI for query optimization. We represented
		queries as graphs and tried to figure out what our models actually learned, where they took shortcuts,
		and where they fell short.
	</p>

	<p>
		That question of "what is the model actually doing?" has stuck with me. I'm not interested in just throwing
		AI at problems. I want to understand it and make sure it's providing real value.
	</p>

	<h3>What I Do</h3>

	<p>
		At Deloitte, I work on infrastructure and backend systems. I'm deep in Python. I wouldn't call myself
		an insane expert, but I know my stuff. I've got certifications in Databricks (Data Engineer Professional)
		and Terraform. The work spans everything from infrastructure-as-code to manual setup on on-prem RHEL
		systems with Ansible.
	</p>

	<p>
		Right now I'm focusing more on Python engineering and starting to dabble in Rust and Mojo for when
		I need more performance. I'm also getting into CUDA because, well, if you're serious about ML, you
		need to understand what's happening closer to the metal.
	</p>

	<h3>What I Care About</h3>

	<p>
		Machine learning is what gets me excited. GenAI is cool but I'm cautious about it. I always want
		to know that what I'm building actually provides value, and that's tougher to ensure with generative models.
		What I really enjoy is staying up to date with research and just dabbling with things. Like figuring out how tools
		like Claude Code can be configured properly for engineering and actually provide consistent value.
	</p>

	<p>
		I created this site to write about things I'm curious about, things I'm reading or working on, or things that matter to me.
		Not to build a brand or chase engagement metrics. Just to think through ideas and share what I learn.
	</p>

	<h3>Outside of Work</h3>

	<p>
		I like going dancing with my girlfriend. I also think a lot about building a meaningful life without
		getting lost in hustle culture, even when you're ambitious. It's a balance I'm still figuring out,
		but I think it's important to actually enjoy the journey.
	</p>

	<p>
		I try to speak plainly and be honest. I can't stand it when people can't
		say what they think or are disingenuous. So that's what you'll get here. My actual thoughts, plainly said.
	</p>
</Layout>
